{
 "source": "XMLUnit's whitespace handling as XmlStringMatcher configures it (ignoreWhitespace, normalizeWhitespace, then ignoreComments): each DOM text, CDATA, attribute and processing-instruction value is String.trim()med (chars up to U+0020) and its Character.isWhitespace runs collapsed to one space, which leaves the no-break spaces (U+00A0, U+2007, U+202F) and U+0085 alone; comments go afterwards, joining the trimmed texts around them. Plain text, attributes, processing instructions, CDATA and an isDateTime placeholder.",
